  "title": "Weather",
  "description": "Talk about seasons, temperatures, and common weather conditions in Chinese.",
  "guidebook": "### Talking About the Weather\n\nTo ask about the weather, say **今天天气怎么样？** (*Jīntiān tiānqì zěnmeyàng?* - How is the weather today?).\n\n### Adjectives Don't Need \"To Be\"\nIn Chinese, you link nouns directly to adjectives using degree adverbs like **很** (*hěn*, very) instead of **是** (*shì*):\n- **今天很冷。** (*Jīntiān hěn lěng.* - Today is cold.)\n- Avoid saying *今天是冷*!\n\nTo express extremes, use **太...了** (*tài... le*, too...):\n- **夏天太热了！** (*Xiàtiān tài rè le!* - Summer is too hot!)\n\n### Rain and Snow Fall Down\nPrecipitation verbs use **下** (*xià*, to fall/descend):\n- **下雨** (*xià yǔ* - to rain)\n- **下雪** (*xià xuě* - to snow)",
